## Deployment

Build the static client using `npm run build` and deploy `dist/` to a static host with SPA fallback enabled. Deploy the Express service to a Node host and provision a managed MySQL database; configure environment variables in the host dashboard, run Prisma migrations during release, and set the production `CLIENT_ORIGIN` and `JWT_SECRET`.

## Authentication and API notes

The API hashes passwords with bcrypt and issues short-lived signed JWTs. Protected routes require an `Authorization: Bearer` token and check project membership or task assignment. Set a unique `JWT_SECRET` of at least 32 characters. Before public deployment, add rate limiting, refresh/session rotation, email verification, robust account recovery, and API integration tests. The frontend currently has no login/register screens and uses local storage instead of API auth. The invite flow copies an in-app link; it does not send email.

## Tests

`npm run test` runs the Vitest domain suite. It covers task creation/update, status transitions, overdue behavior, and project membership checks. API integration tests for registration, task CRUD, and authorization are still needed before production deployment.

In the implementation environment, the domain checks were also run directly with Node and passed. A Vite build and the Vitest runner could not be launched there because npm was unavailable.
